     "question": "Excess CaC2 reacts with 10 g of water to form ethyne (CaC2 + 2H2O -> C2H2 + Ca(OH)2), assuming 100% yield. What mass of ethyne forms? Mr H2O 18.0, C2H2 26.0. Options A 7.22 g, B 14.4 g, C 23.4 g, D 28.9 g.",
