     "question": "0.00100 mol of (NH4)2Cr2O7 is heated and 25.2 cm^3 of N2 is formed at laboratory temperature. Using pressure 101 kPa and PV = nRT, find the laboratory temperature in deg C.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "About 33 deg C (about 306 K)",
     "steps": [
      "From the equation, 1 mol of (NH4)2Cr2O7 gives 1 mol of N2, so n(N2) = 0.00100 mol.",
      "Convert volume: 25.2 cm^3 = 25.2 x 10^-6 m^3 = 2.52 x 10^-5 m^3.",
      "Convert pressure: 101 kPa = 101000 Pa.",
      "Rearrange PV = nRT: T = PV / nR = (101000 x 2.52 x 10^-5) / (0.00100 x 8.31).",
      "T = 2.5452 / 0.00831 = 306 K.",
      "Convert to Celsius: 306 - 273 = 33 deg C."
     ],
