     "question": "10.68 g of hydrated copper(II) sulfate (M = 249.6 g mol-1) dissolves to give 55.0 g of solution; temperature falls from 21.0 C to 18.5 C. Specific heat capacity of solution = 3.70 J g-1 C-1. Calculate the enthalpy change with sign, units and suitable s.f.",
