     "question": "1 kg of petrol is assumed to be pure octane, with standard enthalpy change of combustion -5470 kJ mol-1. The energy used to move the car is 11 MJ. Calculate the percentage of the maximum energy that is available to move the car.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "About 23% (22.9%)",
     "steps": [
      "Molar mass of octane, C8H18 = (8 x 12.0) + (18 x 1.0) = 114 g mol-1.",
      "Moles of octane in 1000 g = 1000 / 114 = 8.77 mol.",
      "Maximum energy from 1 kg = 8.77 x 5470 kJ = approx. 48 000 kJ = 48.0 MJ.",
      "Percentage available = (11 / 48.0) x 100 = 22.9%, which is about 23%."
     ],
