     "question": "For rate = k[NO]^2[O2], which statement is NOT correct? A third order overall; B rate units mol dm-3 s-1; C rate increases when pressure increases; D doubling [NO] and quadrupling [O2] increases rate by a factor of 8.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "D - the rate increases by a factor of 16, not 8",
     "steps": [
      "Overall order = 2 + 1 = 3, so A is correct.",
      "Rate is always in mol dm-3 s-1, so B is correct.",
      "Increasing pressure of gases increases concentration, so the rate increases; C is correct.",
      "Doubling [NO] gives 2^2 = 4; quadrupling [O2] gives 4. Factor = 4 x 4 = 16, not 8.",
      "So statement D is the incorrect one."
     ],
