     "question": "The hydrolysis of RX in aqueous alkali has rate = k[RX]. Which statement is true? Options: A mechanism involves a carbocation intermediate, B SN2 mechanism, C RX could be 1-bromobutane, D the main nucleophile is H2O.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "A - the mechanism involves a carbocation intermediate",
     "steps": [
      "Rate = k[RX] is first order in RX only, so the mechanism is SN1.",
      "SN1 proceeds via a carbocation intermediate, so A is true.",
      "SN2 would have a rate equation involving [OH-], so B is false.",
      "1-bromobutane is primary and reacts by SN2, so C is false; OH- is the nucleophile, so D is false."
     ],
