     "question": "10 mol of N2O4 is placed in a closed container at 50 C. At equilibrium 27% of the N2O4 has dissociated and the pressure is 4.0 atm. Calculate Kp at 50 C.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Kp = 1.26 atm",
     "steps": [
      "Dissociated N2O4 = 27% of 10 mol = 2.7 mol; so N2O4 left = 7.3 mol and NO2 formed = 2 x 2.7 = 5.4 mol.",
      "Total moles at equilibrium = 7.3 + 5.4 = 12.7 mol.",
      "p(N2O4) = 7.3 / 12.7 x 4.0 = 2.30 atm; p(NO2) = 5.4 / 12.7 x 4.0 = 1.70 atm.",
      "Kp = (1.70)^2 / 2.30 = 2.89 / 2.30 = 1.26 atm."
     ],
