     "question": "0.200 mol ethanoic acid and 0.150 mol ethanol reach equilibrium at 25 deg C. The equilibrium mixture needs 34.8 cm^3 of 2.50 mol dm^-3 NaOH to neutralise its ethanoic acid. Calculate Kc.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "Kc = 3.97 (dimensionless)",
     "steps": [
      "Moles of acid at equilibrium = 0.0348 x 2.50 = 0.0870 mol (1:1 with NaOH)",
      "Ester and water formed = 0.200 - 0.0870 = 0.113 mol each",
      "Ethanol at equilibrium = 0.150 - 0.113 = 0.0370 mol",
      "Kc = [ester][water] / ([acid][ethanol]) = (0.113 x 0.113) / (0.0870 x 0.0370)",
      "Volume cancels (2 mol on each side), so Kc = 0.012769 / 0.003219 = 3.97"
     ],
