     "question": "Cl2(aq) reacts with excess KI to give I2, which is titrated with thiosulfate. Using a 10.0 cm3 sample with Cl2 between 0.038 and 0.042 mol dm-3, what thiosulfate concentration gives a titre of about 20 cm3? A 0.010, B 0.020, C 0.040, D 0.080 (mol dm-3).",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "C 0.040 mol dm-3",
     "steps": [
      "Take Cl2 = 0.040 mol dm-3, so n(Cl2) = 0.040 x 0.0100 = 4.0 x 10^-4 mol.",
      "Cl2 + 2I- -> 2Cl- + I2, so n(I2) = 4.0 x 10^-4 mol.",
      "I2 + 2S2O3 2- -> 2I- + S4O6 2-, so n(S2O3 2-) = 2 x 4.0 x 10^-4 = 8.0 x 10^-4 mol.",
      "Concentration = 8.0 x 10^-4 / 0.0200 dm3 = 0.040 mol dm-3."
     ],
