     "question": "350 cm3 of arsine at 115 000 Pa and 20 C reacts with 488 cm3 of 0.102 mol dm-3 cerium(IV) sulfate, forming arsenic. Calculate the final oxidation state of the cerium ion.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "+3 (Ce4+ is reduced to Ce3+)",
     "steps": [
      "Moles of arsine: n = PV/RT = (115 000 x 3.50 x 10^-4) / (8.31 x 293) = 0.0165 mol.",
      "Each AsH3 loses 3 electrons, so electrons lost = 3 x 0.0165 = 0.0496 mol.",
      "Moles of Ce4+ = 0.102 x 0.488 = 0.0498 mol.",
      "Electrons gained per Ce = 0.0496 / 0.0498 = 1.00, so each Ce gains one electron.",
      "Ce4+ + e- -> Ce3+, so the final oxidation state of cerium is +3."
     ],
