     "question": "11.4 g of spinach is treated with 50.0 cm3 of 0.0100 mol dm-3 acidified KMnO4, which oxidises all the ethanedioate ions. The excess MnO4- is titrated with 25.95 cm3 of 0.0500 mol dm-3 acidified Fe2+. Calculate the percentage by mass of CaC2O4 in the spinach.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "0.676 %",
     "steps": [
      "Total MnO4- = 0.0100 x 0.0500 = 5.00 x 10^-4 mol.",
      "Excess MnO4- = (0.0500 x 0.02595) / 5 = 2.595 x 10^-4 mol, since MnO4- + 5Fe2+ is 1:5.",
      "MnO4- used by ethanedioate = 5.00 x 10^-4 - 2.595 x 10^-4 = 2.405 x 10^-4 mol.",
      "2MnO4- + 5C2O4 2- + 16H+ -> 2Mn2+ + 10CO2 + 8H2O, so n(C2O4 2-) = 5/2 x 2.405 x 10^-4 = 6.01 x 10^-4 mol.",
      "Mass of CaC2O4 = 6.01 x 10^-4 x 128.1 = 0.0770 g (Mr 128.1).",
      "Percentage = 0.0770 / 11.4 x 100 = 0.676 %."
     ],
