     "question": "E-zero for Cr3+/Cr is -0.74 V. Calculate the electrode potential at 298 K when [Cr3+] = 0.0100 mol dm-3.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "E = -0.78 V",
     "steps": [
      "Half-equation: Cr3+ + 3e- -> Cr, so n = 3.",
      "Nernst equation: E = E-zero + (RT/nF) ln[Cr3+].",
      "RT/nF = (8.31 x 298)/(3 x 96500) = 0.00855 V.",
      "ln(0.0100) = -4.61, so the correction is 0.00855 x -4.61 = -0.039 V.",
      "E = -0.74 + (-0.039) = -0.78 V."
     ],
