     "question": "A 5.000 g sample of Prince's metal is dissolved and diluted to 250 cm3. 10.0 cm3 aliquots are titrated with 0.100 mol dm-3 thiosulfate; mean titre 22.65 cm3. Calculate the percentage of copper by mass.",
     "status": "ready",
     "answer": "71.9% Cu (3 s.f.)",
     "steps": [
      "Moles thiosulfate = 0.100 x 0.02265 = 2.265 x 10^-3 mol.",
      "I2 : S2O3 2- = 1 : 2, so moles I2 = 1.133 x 10^-3 mol.",
      "Cu2+ : I2 = 2 : 1, so moles Cu2+ in 10.0 cm3 = 2.265 x 10^-3 mol.",
      "In 250 cm3: 2.265 x 10^-3 x 25 = 0.05663 mol Cu.",
      "Mass Cu = 0.05663 x 63.5 = 3.596 g.",
      "Percentage = 3.596 / 5.000 x 100 = 71.9%."
     ],
